 """
 module ProximalBase
 
+# A function of this module with the name of Base's: it shadows Base.ldexp for every call in ProximalBase (Base.ldexp is
+# neither extended nor modified). Base's ldexp(::BigFloat, n) is the exact mpfr_mul_2si only for a Clong n; for any other
+# Integer it is x * exp2(BigFloat(n)), which overflows when 2^n alone leaves the range although x·2^n is representable and
+# rounds n itself at a low precision. A C long is 32 bits on Windows, where an Int shift is not a Clong. MPFR's exponent
+# range lies within a Clong, so a shift saturated at the Clong limits overflows or underflows exactly as it should.
+@inline ldexp(x, n) = Base.ldexp(x, n)
+@inline ldexp(x::BigFloat, n::Integer) = Base.ldexp(x, Clong(clamp(n, typemin(Clong), typemax(Clong))))
+
 using LinearAlgebra
 using SparseArrays
 using LinearAlgebra: LAPACKException, checksquare
